<title>HONG KONG: Trans-Pacific remains Hong Kong's biggest export market.</title>
<headline>Trans-Pacific remains Hong Kong's biggest export market.</headline>
<byline>Jim Gilchrist</byline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The United States and Canada was Hong Kong's biggest pre-Christmas regional export market for air freight, latest Civil Aviation Department statistics show.</p>
<p>Total air cargo handled in December 1996 increased by 13.47 percent compared to the same month last year with 70,574 tonnes of imports and 74,8875 tonnes of exports.</p>
<p>U.S. and Canada accounted for 15,363 tonnes of exports while most imports came from South East Asian countries, 15,947 tonnes.</p>
<p>Regional figures (rounded) in tonnes are shown in the table below in alphabetical order.</p>
<p>			DECEMBER 1996 - ALL FLIGHTS</p>
<p>			    Unloaded    Loaded    Pct change</p>
<p>							  from Dec 95</p>
<p>							  for all cargo</p>
<p> Africa			230	   252	30.4pct</p>
<p> Asia-others	     4,701	 4,891	11.3</p>
<p> Australasia	     5,217	 2,597	1.1</p>
<p> Continental Europe   11,621	10,223	4.7</p>
<p> Japan		     7,976	10,910	9.9</p>
<p> Mainland China	  1,917	 3,542	1.1</p>
<p> Middle East	     1,385	 1,728     41.9</p>
<p> SE Asia		  15,959	12,242     16.5</p>
<p> South America		60	    85     35.7</p>
<p> Taiwan		   10,686	 9,325     28.2</p>
<p> UK			  4,118	 3,634	8.1</p>
<p> USA/Canada		6,705	15,455     18.4</p>
<p> Total		    70,575	74,885     13.5</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax:5017</p>
</text>
